#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1725
msgid ""
"It works for subprocess commands as well. Behavior depends on whether the "
"name is a **binary** on ``$PATH`` or an **alias**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1728
msgid ""
"For a binary, ``?`` prints just the resolved path; ``??`` additionally runs "
"``man``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1731
msgid ""
"@ whoami?\n"
"Resolved whoami: '/usr/bin/whoami'\n"
"\n"
"@ whoami??\n"
"Resolved whoami: '/usr/bin/whoami'\n"
"Running man whoami\n"
"WHOAMI(1)                   General Commands Manual                  "
"WHOAMI(1)\n"
"…"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1742
msgid ""
"When the name does not resolve to any binary, ``??`` no longer falls through "
"to ``man`` — the failed resolution is printed on its own line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1745
msgid ""
"@ nosuch?\n"
"Resolved nosuch: None"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1750
msgid ""
"For an alias, ``?`` gives a short summary and ``??`` adds the docstring, "
"threadable/capturable flags (when set), the source file location and — the "
"new bit — **the function source code** for callable aliases, fetched via "
"``inspect.getsource``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1755
msgid ""
"@ ls?\n"
"Alias: ['ls', '-G']\n"
"\n"
"@ xonfig?\n"
"Alias: <xonsh.xonfig.XonfigAlias>\n"
"Descr: Manage xonsh configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1764
msgid "Define a callable alias and ask for the super-help form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1766
msgid ""
"@ # ~/.xonshrc\n"
"  @aliases.register\n"
"  def _greet(args):\n"
"      \"\"\"Print a friendly greeting.\"\"\"\n"
"      print(\"hello,\", *args)\n"
"\n"
"@ greet?\n"
"Alias: FuncAlias({'name': 'greet', 'func': '_greet', 'return_what': "
"'result'})\n"
"Descr: Print a friendly greeting.\n"
"\n"
"@ greet??\n"
"Alias: FuncAlias({'name': 'greet', 'func': '_greet', 'return_what': "
"'result'})\n"
"Descr: Print a friendly greeting.\n"
"Source: /home/snail/.xonshrc:1\n"
"Code:\n"
"@aliases.register\n"
"def _greet(args):\n"
"    \"\"\"Print a friendly greeting.\"\"\"\n"
"    print(\"hello,\", *args)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1788
msgid ""
"List-style aliases expand recursively through other aliases, and you can see "
"where the leading token resolves on disk:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1791
msgid ""
"@ aliases['lst']  = ['ls', '-la']\n"
"@ aliases['lst2'] = ['lst', '/tmp']\n"
"@ lst2??\n"
"Alias: ['lst', '/tmp']\n"
"Expanded: ['ls', '-G', '-la', '/tmp']\n"
"Resolved ls: '/opt/homebrew/.../ls'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial.rst:1800
msgid ""
"For callable aliases defined interactively in the REPL, ``inspect`` has no "
"source file to read from (``co_filename`` is ``<stdin>``), so ``Code:`` is "
"replaced with a ``<source unavailable>`` placeholder while ``Source:`` still "
"shows where the function was declared."
msgstr ""

